  "title_en": "Simulated bench extension - 30 nodes in three sectors",
  "provenance": "SYNTHETIC MODEL of the simulated extension to an indoor bench: three radio sectors, each a star around an access point with a store-and-forward chain reaching a field device, over a fibre backbone and a private LTE overlay. Simulated nodes carry explicit coordinates, which is why a distance-based heuristic remains admissible here and would not be on the conducted rig, where cable length does not bound transport cost. Identifiers, coordinates and link qualities are invented for this exercise and contain nothing from any laboratory's inventory, addressing or configuration.",
  "coordinate_system": "Local planar grid in metres; origin at the operations centre. Distances are Euclidean and DERIVED from these coordinates, never stored separately, so the geometry and the A* heuristic can never disagree.",
